   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK - Foreign, Commonwealth Development Office (FCDO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Macro Political Economy Analysis, Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UK&#x2019;s overarching goal for a productive partnership with Nigeria is stated in the Partnership summary: &#x201c;The UK&#x2019;s objective in Nigeria is to support a more stable, inclusive, resilient, healthy, and prosperous Nigeria that sees the UK as a strategic partner for peace, climate action, trade, and development&quot;. This scoping work will enable an understanding of the constraints to formulating good policies; identifying constraints beyond the visible, aids in that design process. The second gain of a good and well written PEA is how relationships are mapped out. This allows the engagement process on policies that can lead to reforms to be deeper and less theoretical. Then there is the issue of policy correlation that address issues that deepen poverty and exacerbate violence. While the current approach to stemming this violence by the government is &#x201c;boots on ground&#x201d; the PEA can give an indication on why there is an absence of thought on linkages. 

This political economy analysis will hope to: 
&#x2022;	Identify sectors with productive potential, especially in terms of contributing to broad-based, inclusive employment. 
&#x2022;	Identify governance challenges in (selected) key areas identified by the country plan 
&#x2022;	Provide analysis that will help the FCDO triangulate evidence for its programmatic decisions.</narrative>
  </description>
